```md
Created and installed **`$engineering` v0.1.0**, combining all **11 local `engineering-*` skills** into one self-contained skill.

It provides one entry point with internal references for each mode. You can name a mode explicitly or let it select the modes needed for the task. It does **not** run every workflow as a mandatory pipeline.

| Included mode | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Task framing | Establish purpose, scope, authority, and success evidence |
| Adaptive discovery | Resolve unknowns one question at a time |
| Non-adaptive discovery | Present one fixed questionnaire and synthesize the answers |
| Decomposition | Map responsibilities, dependencies, interfaces, and constraints |
| Assumption audit | Separate evidence, assumptions, conventions, and unknowns |
| Decision premortem | Compare options through independent future-failure analysis |
| Red team | Challenge a plan’s credible failure paths |
| Reconstruction | Rebuild alternatives from evidence that survived scrutiny |
| Experiment design | Define a bounded test with predeclared outcomes |
| Execution protocol | Carry out authorized changes, verify, and hand off |
| Deliverable contract | Produce and check an artifact against its required form |

The bundle preserves the modes’ boundaries: decomposition stays analysis-only, fixed questionnaires stay fixed, and analysis or experiment design does not grant permission to execute changes. All 11 original skills remain unchanged and available separately.

Use it like this:

```text
Use $engineering to work through this engineering task.

Use $engineering in red-team mode to review this plan.

Use $engineering with non-adaptive discovery to gather the
requirements for this migration.
```

